{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793472387,"nonce":"82TgQ9jcBwAK43rmqUObNljIx9w=","title":"cn behaviour parity with ashui: keyboard and pointer behaviour the migrated components lack","message":"Style parity is largely done; behaviour is not checked as thoroughly. Found while comparing ashui's component docs and sources with cn.\n\nFixed (1aedeaf2): clicking the trigger of an open dropdown menu or popover reopened it; number input has no wheel stepping; Escape did not clear a search field.\n\nStill missing in cn:\n- DropdownMenu: ashui focuses the first item when opened from the keyboard (the panel itself when opened by a press) and navigates with Arrow Up/Down, Home and End, Enter selects, Escape closes; Menubar also switches menus on Left/Right. cn's menu has no keyboard navigation.\n- Select and Combobox: keyboard open, arrow navigation, Enter to choose, typeahead; the combobox search should keep focus while Arrows/Home/End reveal the selected row (ashui Command does).\n- Switch, Checkbox, Radio, Toggle: focus stop, Space/Enter to toggle, :focus-visible ring (needs the input-modality work in e4d2db3).\n- NumberInput: ashui also lets an active parent scroll keep its gesture (momentum) when the control moves under the pointer, with a 250 ms wheel gap before a new gesture edits the value.\n- Input: a leading/trailing icon part (clicking it focuses the field).\n\nLow priority, per the user: switch thumb easing (ashui uses --ease-spring for the thumb, cn uses --ease-state to avoid overshoot), the select chevron rotating while open, and the switch's state icons fading. A switch toggled inside a use_state_keyed build function showed no rebuild in the headless runner (same node, no build-generation change), so any rebuild the user sees in the windowed runner is specific to that path: not reproduced.\n\nEach item wants a headless test of the behaviour (keys through Headless once keyboard input exists there: b79b754), not just a golden.\n\nRelated: e4d2db3, b79b754, 5f0c8eb.","files":null}]}